Hi,

I was thinking about ¹) kconfig to display potentially useful infos out
of OE recipe metadata.

As you can see, this incarnation uses pn instead of packages and just
emits depends as select. Furthermore it does nothing useful with the
output, just displays it grouped by section. As said, it's just random
thought for now.
Now my question is if there is interrest in doing something like this
and if so, how to represent the data. One could think about adding
LICENSE filters, for example. One could write a package-list out that
could serve as 'bitbake $(cat my-list.txt)' and so on. If people like
the idea and if we can come up with something that we can represent with
some easy-to-use tool then it could potentially useful for users, i
guess.

Ideas?

Ok, but on to my rant :)
- BBMASK = "(libqglviewer)"
  Bitbake does not handle inline comments, i.e. FOO="BAR" # comment
  The package above contains inline comments and should be fixed (or
  bitbake should be extended; uncool since potentially slows down
  line reading. I'll leave my fingers off slowing down bitbake.)
- SECTION clutter. See attached section-overview.txt
  There are quite some sections that "shadow" sections with more
  entries, for example the whole "application" submenu (with pythm in
  multimedia). Same for the whole "applications" submenu (with nrlolsr)

  I want to ask people to cleanup the sections. Perhaps we could
  structure them better -- base is pretty crowded.

¹) http://busybox.net/~aldot/bitbake/ the 3 fwd-kconfig.00l2* files

--xHFwDpU9dbj6ez1V
